WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
"I goed to the park!"

2
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.710
A toddler tells her dad all about her day.

3
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.980
Now listen to her family at dinner.

4
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.490
Mum went to work.

5
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.460
Grandad went to the shops.

6
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.240
Nobody says goed.

7
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.120
No one taught her a
rule for the past tense.

8
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.190
So where did goed come from?

9
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.670
Whose rule is it?

10
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.940
In this mission, you'll meet Skinner,
who said children learn by copying what

11
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.590
they hear, and by being rewarded.

12
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.310
You'll meet Chomsky, who argued that children
are born with a capacity for grammar.

13
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.050
And Bruner, who looked at how adults'
talk supports a child as she learns.

14
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.100
Your mission: work out
whose rule 'goed' really is.
